[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Python Control Flow: if, elif, else"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Control flow statements determine the order in which code is executed. Python provides 'if', 'elif' (else if), and 'else' statements to create conditional logic."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"The 'if' Statement"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"The 'if' statement executes a block of code only if a specified condition is true. The condition is an expression that evaluates to either True or False."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"age = 20
if age >= 18:
    print("You are an adult.")"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"In this example, the code inside the 'if' block will execute because the condition 'age >= 18' is true."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"The 'else' Statement"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"The 'else' statement provides an alternative block of code to execute if the 'if' condition is false."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"age = 16
if age >= 18:
    print("You are an adult.")
else:
    print("You are a minor.")"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"Here, the 'else' block will execute because 'age >= 18' is false."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"The 'elif' Statement"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"The 'elif' (else if) statement allows you to check multiple conditions in sequence. It's placed between the 'if' and 'else' statements."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"score = 75
if score >= 90:
    print("Excellent!")
elif score >= 70:
    print("Good job!")
elif score >= 50:
    print("You passed.")
else:
    print("Needs improvement.")"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"In this case, the 'elif score >= 70:' condition is met, so "Good job!" will be printed."},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Nesting 'if', 'elif', and 'else' Statements"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can nest 'if', 'elif', and 'else' statements within each other to create more complex decision-making logic."},{"order":17,"type":"code","text":"x = 10
y = 5
if x > 0:
    if y > 0:
        print("Both x and y are positive.")
    else:
        print("x is positive, but y is not.")
else:
    print("x is not positive.")"},{"order":18,"type":"subheading","text":"Important Considerations"},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Indentation is crucial in Python. The code within each block ('if', 'elif', 'else') must be indented correctly."},{"order":20,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Conditions are evaluated from top to bottom. Once a condition is true, the corresponding block is executed, and the remaining conditions are skipped."},{"order":21,"type":"bullet_point","text":"You can use logical operators ('and', 'or', 'not') to combine multiple conditions."},{"order":22,"type":"code","text":"age = 25
has_license = True
if age >= 18 and has_license:
    print("Can drive.")
else:
    print("Cannot drive.")"}]
